<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50625" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴουλος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], ὁ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>down, the first growth of the whiskers and beard</i>,
			in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρίν σφωϊν ὑπὸ κροτάφοισιν ἰούλους
					ἀνθῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.319
				</span></i>
			: later in sg., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στείχει δ᾽ ἴ. ἄρτι διὰ παρηΐδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					534
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶτον ἴ. ἀπὸ κροτ άφων καταβάλλειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					15.85
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτι χνοάοντας ἰούλους ἀντ έλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.43
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ κροτάφοισιν ἰούλους κειράμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.198
				</span></i>
			 (Antip. Thess.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰούλοις πλῆσαι παρειάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1601
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>corn-sheaf</i>, whence Demeter is said to be named <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰουλώ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Semus
				19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Carm.Pop.</u>
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>song in honour of Demeter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Semus
			</span></i> l.c., Apollod.Hist.<i><span class="en">
				149
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>catkin</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.5.5
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.7.3
			</span></i>; <i>tendril</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				3.18.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>creature like the centipede</i>, prob. the <i>wood-louse</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				523b18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				682b3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				19
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				959
			</span></i>; <i>earthworm</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Numen.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.305a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰουλίς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				12
			</span></i> (pl.). (Perh. cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖλος</span>, q.v.)</div>
